Spec: Project/Architecture

Purpose:
  Describes how the project's OWN components (layers, modules, stack) are
   structured and connected — this is the project's technical architecture,
   NOT the .sdd system's own meta-architecture (see architecture/architecture.sdd
   — different, separate document, STEP 3), NOT global engineering-architecture
   principles (modularity, coupling, dependency direction) — those live in
   architecture/principles.sdd (STEP 13) and concrete layer relationships
   (Rules/Validation below) are checked against those global rules
   (see Resolution: architecture/principles.sdd -> Resolution).

Layers:
  DB
  BE
  API
  FE
  MD
  QA
  DO

Rules:
  Architecture relationships MUST be explicit.
  Forbidden dependencies MUST be declared.
  Architecture violations MUST be detectable.
  Architecture changes require human decision (bax PROJECT.sdd -> [R9]/[R11]).

Validation:
  implemented_structure MUST conform to declared architecture.

State:
  + = compliant
  ! = violation
  ? = architecture decision required
  ~ = architecture change in progress

ViolationVsDecision:
  AI MUST NOT silently resolve which of these two cases occurred:
    A) mistake                 -> state: ! (Architecture Violation)
    B) deliberate new decision -> state: ? (Architecture Decision Required,
                                   human approval, see PROJECT.sdd HumanDecision)
  AI leaves `?` and stops — it does NOT mark `!` saying "not fixing", nor
  does it silently accept as new normal.

Note:
  This document is a SCHEMA — concrete layer relationships (e.g. BE -> DB,
  FE -> API) are generated per project from templates/_sdd/architecture/.
  This file does not contain concrete project data.

State: +
